  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ Society for Equality - OUR VOICES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant applied by Society for Equality (S4E) aims to contribute to sure that women and girls are given the same rights and opportunities as men in the societies in which they live. The Project titled &quot;Our Voices Must Be Heard&quot; by S4E Will, intends to reduce all Forms Of Gender-Based Violence (GBV) from society in both rural and urban settings. In order to execute the project, the team is intends to take steps to ensure that women and girls of reproductive age become more self-reliant and capable of speaking out againstall forms of violence and achieving the fundamental rights to which they are entitled as women through various empowerment activities. Such as conducting entrepreneurship training for two groups of 20 people - skills on the saloon, horticulture, food vendor, tailoring skills, organisation and staff capacity building and strengthening, and sensitisation on GBV issues in the project area. the project will be implemented in different modalities, such as a campaign will be conducted in the form of offline and online. also, the project intends to create a documentary

Among other, the below activities will be implemented by S4E, the activities include:
Activity 1: Organization and Staff capacity building and Strengthening
Activity 2: Project Inception and Sensitization on GBV Issue in the project area
Activity 3: Entrepreneurship Training for two groups of 20 people - Skill on Saloon, Horticulture, Food vendor and Tailoring skills
Activity 4: Offline and Online Campaign
Activity 5: Organize and develop a documentary</narrative>
  </description>
