  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Society for Equality</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Society for Equality. A community-based organization known as S4e was established in the year 2021 by a group of female residents of the city of Mwanza. The abbreviation &quot;S4e&quot; stands for the &quot;Society for Equality.&quot; The primary objective was to improve the economic standing of young women and girls, as well as to provide the groups with rights regarding sexual and reproductive health care.In addition, the goal was to provide the groups with sexual and reproductive health rights. In addition to that, the objective was to enhance the economic standing of the groups. 2021 was the year that official registration for S4e took place, and the organization&#xa0;was given the registration number Mcc/Cd/Shg/885. S4e was able to successfully draft a constitution, which at this point acts as the basis for the community-based organization as well as all activities. The group originally operated as a charitable organization when it was founded. The primary objectives are to impart leadership and self-confidence skills to young girls and women, to raise awareness and provide training on sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR), and to provide vocational training and skills foraspiring entrepreneurs.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
